  "topic": "Read and write Lam (ل) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Lam. Like 'l' in 'lamp' or 'love'. Tongue tip touches behind upper teeth a liquid sound!",
      "title": "Meet Lam!",
      "ar": "ل",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Lam"
    },
    {
      "en": "A tall, elegant upward curve that flows to the right, like a shepherd's crook. Lam is elegant and tall like the Lam-Alef ligature which means 'No' in Arabic!",
      "title": "How to write Lam"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Lam says “la”.",
      "title": "Lam with fatha",
      "ar": "لَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Lam says “le”.",
      "title": "Lam with kasra",
      "ar": "لِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Lam says “lo”.",
      "title": "Lam with damma",
      "ar": "لُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“The Arabic language is beautiful”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "اللُّغَةُ العَرَبِيَّةُ جَمِيلَة",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Al-Lughatu Al-Arabiyyatu Jamila"
    }
  ],
